### Works in IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) and VS Code (REST Client extension)
### Run the requests top to bottom. Tokens are stored automatically (IntelliJ syntax).

@host = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Login as teacher
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "teacher@demo.com", "password": "Teacher@123" }

> {% client.global.set("teacherToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2. List subjects (master data)
GET {{host}}/subjects
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### 3. Add a question
POST {{host}}/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Which HTTP method is idempotent?",
  "subjectId": 6,
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "explanation": "PUT can be repeated with the same result.",
  "options": [
    { "text": "POST", "correct": false },
    { "text": "PUT",  "correct": true },
    { "text": "PATCH", "correct": false }
  ]
}

### 4. Search questions
GET {{host}}/questions?subjectId=1&difficulty=EASY&page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### 5. Create an exam (DRAFT) - use real question ids from step 4
POST {{host}}/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maths Quick Quiz",
  "durationMinutes": 15,
  "startTime": "2026-01-01T09:00:00",
  "endTime": "2030-12-31T18:00:00",
  "showResultImmediately": true,
  "questions": [
    { "questionId": 1, "positiveMarks": 4, "negativeMarks": 1 },
    { "questionId": 2, "positiveMarks": 4, "negativeMarks": 1 }
  ]
}

### 6. Publish the exam (replace 2 with the id returned above)
POST {{host}}/exams/2/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

### 7. Assign exam to classroom 1
POST {{host}}/classrooms/1/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "examIds": [2] }

### 8. Login as student
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "student1@demo.com", "password": "Student@123" }

> {% client.global.set("studentToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 9. My exams
GET {{host}}/student/exams
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 10. Start exam 1 (returns the paper without correct answers)
POST {{host}}/student/exams/1/start
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 11. Submit answers (use real option ids from step 10)
POST {{host}}/student/exams/1/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answers": [
    { "questionId": 1, "selectedOptionId": 3, "timeSpentSeconds": 20 },
    { "questionId": 2, "selectedOptionId": 6, "timeSpentSeconds": 15 }
  ]
}

### 12. My detailed result
GET {{host}}/student/results/1
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 13. Leaderboard + analytics (teacher)
GET {{host}}/exams/1/leaderboard
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/exams/1/analytics
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherToken}}
